## Installation

Install `{{ distribution_name }}` using [pip](https://pip.pypa.io/) or [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/):

```
pip install {{ distribution_name }}
```

## Development

Install [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/getting-started/installation/) and
create a virtual environment:

```bash
uv venv
source .venv/bin/activate
```

Install the package and its development dependencies:

```bash
uv lock
uv sync --group dev{% if docs %} --group docs{% endif %}
```

Commit `uv.lock` with the project. Run the test suite and checks with:

```bash
make test
make lint
make typecheck
make build
make check-dist
```
{% if tasks == "nox" %}
Use `make nox` for the supported-Python test matrix and
`uv run noxfile.py -s tests-3.13 -- tests/` for a focused Nox run.
{% endif -%}
{% if docs %}
Use `make docs` for a strict documentation build and `make docs-serve` for
the local preview. GitHub Pages deployment requires configuring the repository
to use GitHub Actions as its Pages source.
{% endif %}
